# Build context exclusions — Zamorin Cafe ERP
#
# Most important entry: backend/node_modules. Without it, `COPY backend ./backend`
# overwrites the image's own node_modules with the host's build, which is
# frequently a different platform/ABI and breaks native modules (bcrypt).

**/node_modules
**/.git

# Secrets must never enter the build context.
backend/.env
backend/.env.*
!backend/.env.example
!backend/.env.production.example

# Test and QA output — not needed at runtime.
backend/test
backend/tests
backend/test-results
backend/test_files_audit.json
backend/test_summary.json
**/*.test.js
**/__tests__

# Native clients are built by separate CI jobs, not this image.
Platform

# Repo noise.
docs
artifacts
scripts
*.md
*.xlsx
*.json
!backend/package.json
!backend/package-lock.json

# The full frontend is served by the caddy container in docker-compose.yml,
# not by this image. Only the logo SVG referenced by companyIdentityService.js
# is pulled in explicitly via COPY, so everything else under frontend/ is
# dropped (~26MB). Docker cannot re-include a path beneath a directory that is
# excluded outright, hence the layer-by-layer negation below.
frontend/*
!frontend/src
frontend/src/*
!frontend/src/assets
frontend/src/assets/*
!frontend/src/assets/zamorin-logo-horizontal.svg
